RUBY
====

Original source can be downloaded from:
https://cache.ruby-lang.org/pub/ruby/4.0/

file   = ruby-4.0.9.tar.xz
sha256 = a8057adb39f51ad6dc3106237504c93dd792bb515837b4fe7817ae21ed7e51f4

Deleted (not needed to build or install Ruby): test/, spec/,
bootstraptest/, benchmark/, sample/, doc/, win32/, wasm/, cygwin/.
No local modifications.

These sources are used in:
	usr.bin/ruby	ruby, irb, gem, erb, ... and libruby.so.40, with
			Ruby's own configure and makefiles (see the comment
			there); the extensions link the base's LibreSSL and
			libyaml.  fiddle (FFI) is not built: libffi is not in
			the base.

The build must not write into this directory: usr.bin/ruby configures
--without-git (else the bundled gems' sources would be cloned into
gems/src) and builds in its object directory.

Ruby's licence: BSD-2-Clause or the Ruby licence (COPYING, BSDL);
LEGAL lists the files with other terms.
